message.content:
{
  "score_support": "supports_wrong_score",
  "score_support_basis": "理由把评论开头的“3) detection heuristics...”当成论文中可精确定位的部分，并据此判为 fully grounded，再叠加特异性推出 5 分；但真实标签为 3，即定位不充分却问题具体，CoT 的证据链主要支撑错误的 5 分。",
  "error_sentences": [
    {
      "sentence": "The comment begins with \"3) detection heuristics for logical reasoning phenomena,\" which explicitly identifies a specific part of the paper (likely a section or subsection).",
      "error_type": "evidence_misread",
      "explanation": "“3)”更可能是审稿人自己的条目编号，待评价文本并未明确指向论文的章节、表、图或唯一部位；“likely a section or subsection”也暴露其只是猜测，不能成立为精确定位。"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "This makes the comment fully grounded, as the authors can precisely locate the referenced part.",
      "error_type": "unsupported_inference",
      "explanation": "由一个推测性的部分指称直接推出作者能精确定位，缺乏材料依据；按真实标签该评论属于作者不能自信定位但问题明确的档位。"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "Therefore, the comment is both fully grounded and specific, meeting the criteria for a score of 5.",
      "error_type": "score_mapping_error",
      "explanation": "5 分要求明确指向且具体；在 grounding 实际较弱、仅 specificity 较强时，应映射到 3 而非 5，结论分数档位与证据不匹配。"
    }
  ],
  "overall_basis": "CoT 误将审稿条目编号/泛化主题当作可精确定位依据，把“弱定位但问题具体”的 3 分情形错推为“定位明确且具体”的 5 分。"
}
